ential equation by $I(t)=(16.5+t)^{0.5}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(16.5+t)^{0.5}\\cdot (\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{0.5}{16.5+t}\\,Q) & =(16.5+t)^{0.5}\\cdot 1.5 \\\\ (16.5+t)^{0.5}\\frac{dQ}{dt}+0.5(16.5+t)^{-0.5}Q & =1.5(16.5+t)^{0.5} \\\\ \\frac{d}{dt}(Q(16.5+t)^{0.5}) & =1.5(16.5+t)^{0.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dt}(Q(16.5+t)^{0.5})\\,dt & =\\int 1.5(16.5+t)^{0.5}\\,dt \\\\ Q(16.5+t)^{0.5} & =1.5\\cdot \\frac{1}{1.5}(16.5+t)^{1.5}+C \\\\ Q(t) & =1(16.5+t)+\\frac{C}{(16.5+t)^{0.5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $\\frac{33}{8}\\,\\text{lb}$ of dye. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=\\frac{33}{8},$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ 1(16.5+0)+\\frac{C}{(16.5+0)^{0.5}} & =\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ 16.5+\\frac{C}{(16.5)^{0.5}} & =\\frac{33}{8} \\\\ \\frac{C}{(16.5)^{0.5}} & =-\\frac{99}{8} \\\\ C & =-\\frac{99}{8}(16.5)^{0.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(t) & =1(16.5+t)-\\frac{\\frac{99}{8}(16.5)^{0.5}}{(16.5+t)^{0.5}} \\\\  & =1(16.5+t)-\\frac{99}{8}{(\\frac{16.5}{16.5+t})}^{0.5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let ${t}_{o}$ be the time when the tank begins to overflow. The tank has a capacity of $82\\,\\text{gal},$ so we can use the condition $V({t}_{o})=82$ to solve for ${t}_{o}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V({t}_{o}) & =82 \\\\ 33+3{t}_{o}-1{t}_{o} & =82 \\\\ 33+2{t}_{o} & =82 \\\\ 2{t}_{o} & =49 \\\\ {t}_{o} & =24.5\\,\\text{min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, rounded to one decimal place, the amount of dye in the tank at the moment it begins to overflow is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(24.5) & =1(16.5+24.5)-\\frac{99}{8}{(\\frac{16.5}{16.5+24.5})}^{0.5} \\\\  & =41-\\frac{99}{8}{(\\frac{16.5}{41})}^{0.5} \\\\  & ≈33.1\\,\\text{lb}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186539438 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539407 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [